.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-BACKUP-PACK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-backup-pack
.Nd send a snapshot of this machine to another host as one compressed ZFS stream
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -host Ar host
.Op Fl -dataset Ar dataset | Fl -full
.Op Fl -dest-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -keep-snapshot
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
takes a recursive snapshot of a dataset, sends it with
.Ql zfs send -R
\(em the dataset, its children and every snapshot in their history \(em
compresses it with
.Xr zstd 1 ,
and writes it over
.Xr ssh 1
to a file on
.Ar host ,
with a small text file of facts about it beside:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
DIR/HOSTNAME-TIMESTAMP.zfs.zst    the stream
DIR/HOSTNAME-TIMESTAMP.meta       where it came from
.Ed
.Pp
The other host needs nothing but
.Xr ssh 1 ,
a shell and room: it stores a file, not a pool.
.Xr kldload-backup-restore 8
brings the file back into a pool, on this machine or another.
.Pp
Without
.Fl -dataset ,
the dataset is the one mounted at
.Pa / ,
the running boot environment
.Pq Pa rpool/ROOT/ Ns Ar name :
the operating system and its configuration.
.Pa /home ,
.Pa /srv ,
the machines under
.Pa rpool/vms
and container storage are datasets of their own beside it, and are not
included; send them with
.Fl -dataset ,
or everything with
.Fl -full .
.Pp
When anything in what is sent is encrypted, as on an install with
encryption, the stream is sent raw
.Pq Ql zfs send -w :
it stays encrypted on the other host, which never needs the key, and
restoring it needs the sender's passphrase or key.
ZFS will not send an encrypted dataset with its properties any other way.
.Pp
The snapshot,
.Ar dataset Ns Pa @backup- Ns Ar TIMESTAMP ,
is removed when the run ends, whether it succeeded or not, unless
.Fl -keep-snapshot .
.Pp
Everything the run prints is also appended to
.Pa /var/log/kldload/backup-pack.log .
It must run as root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -host Ar host
Where the file goes: a host name
.Xr ssh 1
reaches as whoever root is set up to log in as there, or
.Ar user Ns @ Ns Ar host .
Required, unless
.Ev BACKUP_REMOTE_HOST
is set.
.It Fl -dataset Ar dataset
Send this dataset and its children instead of the running root.
.It Fl -full
Send the whole pool the running root is on.
.It Fl -dest-dir Ar dir
The directory on
.Ar host ,
made if missing; an absolute path of letters, digits and
.Ql _ . / + - .
Default
.Pa /var/lib/kldload-backups .
.It Fl -keep-snapshot
Leave the snapshot on this machine after sending.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev BACKUP_REMOTE_HOST
The host when
.Fl -host
is not given.
.It Ev BACKUP_REMOTE_DIR
The directory when
.Fl -dest-dir
is not given.
.It Ev BACKUP_SSH_OPTS
Options for every
.Xr ssh 1
call, split on spaces; default
.Ql -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/backup-pack.log
Every run's output.
.It Ar dir Ns Pa / Ns Ar hostname Ns Pa - Ns Ar timestamp Ns Pa .meta
On
.Ar host :
the source host and dataset, the snapshot, times, sizes, whether the
stream is raw
.Pq Ql send_raw ,
the kldload profile and the kernel.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Sent, and the file on
.Ar host
is not empty.
.It 1
Not root, a tool missing,
.Ar host
unreachable or its directory not writable, or the send failed.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop with an encrypted pool on 2026-09-29.
.Xr ssh 1
was replaced for these runs by a stand-in that runs the remote command on
the same machine, so
.Ql backup1
is this host; everything else is the real tool.
.Ql rpool/bptest-3308726
was made for the purpose and destroyed afterwards.
