.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "[pack] FATAL: cannot reach HOST or write to DIR"
.Xr ssh 1
could not log in with
.Ql BatchMode=yes
\(em no key accepted, or the host is down \(em or the directory could not
be made or written.
.It "[pack] FATAL: send pipeline failed (check ssh + remote disk space)"
The send, the compression or the copy stopped; ZFS's or ssh's reason is
above.
The snapshot is removed.
.It "[pack] FATAL: remote file is empty or missing"
.It "[pack] WARNING: could not remove SNAPSHOT; remove it by hand"
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr zstd 1 ,
.Xr kldload-backup-restore 8 ,
.Xr ksnap 8 ,
.Xr zfs-send 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: no machine with an encrypted pool could
be backed up, since ZFS refuses to send an encrypted dataset with its
properties unless raw; the destination defaulted to one particular host
name,
.Ql fiend ;
host and directory reached
.Xr ssh 1
unchecked; and this tool's own description said
.Pa /home
was sent with the root, which on a kldload install it never was.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Each run is a full stream: nothing is incremental, and every run costs the
whole size again.
.Pp
The check after sending is that the file is there and not empty.
A stream is proved only by receiving it; see
.Xr kldload-backup-restore 8 .
.Pp
A raw stream is useless without the key.
Keep the passphrase somewhere that is not this machine.
.Pp
The other host's key is accepted the first time it is seen
.Pq Ql accept-new
and checked after.
